{ "path": "docs/AI-PRODUCTION-OPERATIONS.md", "hunks": [ { "oldStart": 64, "oldCount": 6, "newStart": 64, "newCount": 6, "header": "@@ -64,6 +64,6 @@ azd provision", "lines": [ { "oldNumber": 64, "newNumber": 64 }, { "oldNumber": 65, "newNumber": 65, "text": "## Diagnostics and telemetry" }, { "oldNumber": 66, "newNumber": 66 }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 67, "text": "Tenant admins and break-glass Super Admins receive only tenant, treatment, timestamp, authorization/validation outcome, safe reason code, provider/deployment/model/region, prompt version, retry count, token counts, estimated cost, latency, and correlation ID. The Super Admin page also aggregates latency, token use, estimated cost, validation/provider failures, safety outcomes, and rate/spend limiting." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 67, "text": "Tenant admins and break-glass Super Admins receive tenant, treatment, timestamp, authorization/validation outcome, safe reason code, provider/deployment/model/region, prompt version, retry count, token counts, estimated cost, latency, correlation ID, and the raw provider response for validation-rejected invocations. The Super Admin page also aggregates latency, token use, estimated cost, validation/provider failures, safety outcomes, and rate/spend limiting." }, { "oldNumber": 68, "newNumber": 68 }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 69, "text": "Raw CRM context, prompts, responses, generated output, source references, placeholder mappings, and tokenised artifacts must never be logged, displayed, or exported as diagnostics or telemetry." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 69, "text": "Raw CRM context, prompts, accepted generated output, source references, placeholder mappings, and tokenised artifacts must never be logged, displayed, or exported as diagnostics or telemetry. A validation-rejected provider response is retained on its tenant-scoped audit event and displayed only in the tenant-admin AI audit or recorded break-glass Super Admin view. It may contain model-generated sensitive content and follows the audit event's retention lifecycle." } ] } ] }
{ "path": "docs/specs/privacy-preserving-ai-relationship-assistance.md", "hunks": [ { "oldStart": 75, "oldCount": 7, "newStart": 75, "newCount": 7, "header": "@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ AI remains assist-only. It may read, classify, summarize, recommend, and draft.", "lines": [ { "oldNumber": 75, "newNumber": 75, "text": "51. As an operator, I want any Global deployment or fallback to require explicit configuration, so that regional behavior cannot change silently." }, { "oldNumber": 76, "newNumber": 76, "text": "52. As an operator, I want managed identity and scoped RBAC for provider access, so that shared API keys are unnecessary." }, { "oldNumber": 77, "newNumber": 77, "text": "53. As an operator, I want aggregate tenant-safe telemetry for latency, tokens, cost, failures, and safety outcomes, so that the service can be operated without logging CRM content." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 78, "text": "54. As an operator, I want redacted diagnostics with correlation IDs and reason codes, so that failures can be investigated without exposing prompts or model output." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 78, "text": "54. As an operator, I want diagnostics with correlation IDs, reason codes, and rejected provider responses, so that validation failures can be investigated from the actual model output." }, { "oldNumber": 79, "newNumber": 79, "text": "55. As an operator, I want bounded concurrency, output size, and retries, so that provider load and spend remain predictable." }, { "oldNumber": 80, "newNumber": 80, "text": "56. As a product owner, I want representative quality and safety checks to pass before production enablement, so that direct rollout has an explicit release gate." }, { "oldNumber": 81, "newNumber": 81 } ] }, { "oldStart": 104, "oldCount": 9, "newStart": 104, "newCount": 9, "header": "@@ -104,9 +104,9 @@ AI remains assist-only. It may read, classify, summarize, recommend, and draft.", "lines": [ { "oldNumber": 104, "newNumber": 104, "text": "- Tenant administrators can view current-period usage and estimated spend. Estimates are clearly labeled and do not claim to be the Azure invoice." }, { "oldNumber": 105, "newNumber": 105, "text": "- AI artifacts are tenant-owned and contact-scoped. They store treatment, lifecycle status, source snapshot identity, tokenised structured artifact, prompt/model/deployment versions, generation and freshness anchors, usage linkage, validation outcome, and safe failure code." }, { "oldNumber": 106, "newNumber": 106, "text": "- Source links are normalized into tenant-owned artifact-source records. The system can determine whether each source still exists, whether the current user may view it, and whether a new eligible item makes an artifact stale." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 107, "text": "- Raw provider requests, raw provider responses, raw CRM context copies, and reversible mappings are never retained. Tokenised artifacts are retained under the tenant's CRM retention policy." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 108, "text": "- Each invocation creates an immutable tenant-scoped audit event containing actor, authorization and enablement outcome, feature/contact, approved source references, placeholder category counts, prompt/model/deployment/region, timestamps, retry count, validation outcome, artifact linkage, usage estimate, safe reason code, and correlation ID. It contains no raw content." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 109, "text": "- Audit events are readable by tenant administrators. Super Admin access is break-glass and exposes only redacted structured diagnostics, never CRM content, mappings, prompts, or model output." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 107, "text": "- Raw provider requests, accepted provider responses, raw CRM context copies, and reversible mappings are never retained. A validation-rejected provider response is retained on its tenant-scoped audit event for administrator diagnosis and follows the audit retention lifecycle. Tokenised artifacts are retained under the tenant's CRM retention policy." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 108, "text": "- Each invocation creates an immutable tenant-scoped audit event containing actor, authorization and enablement outcome, feature/contact, approved source references, placeholder category counts, prompt/model/deployment/region, timestamps, retry count, validation outcome, artifact linkage, usage estimate, safe reason code, correlation ID, and the raw provider response when validation rejects it." }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 109, "text": "- Audit events are readable by tenant administrators. Super Admin access is break-glass and exposes the same validation-rejected provider response after recording a reason; prompts, raw CRM context, and mappings remain excluded." }, { "oldNumber": 110, "newNumber": 110, "text": "- Deleting a tenant purges its AI settings, artifacts, source links, usage records, dismissals, and audit data according to the applicable retention process. Deleting an individual source removes any retained source text and makes existing references render as Source deleted; artifacts are purged when retention rules require it." }, { "oldNumber": 111, "newNumber": 111, "text": "- AI work runs asynchronously through the existing durable background-job infrastructure. Jobs restore and verify tenant scope before tenant-filtered work." }, { "oldNumber": 112, "newNumber": 112, "text": "- Requests deduplicate against treatment, tenant, contact or source message, retrieval-profile version, and source snapshot. An in-progress duplicate returns the existing pending state; a reusable completed artifact avoids a new model call." } ] } ] }
{ "path": "src/AndrewCrm.Web/Data/Entities.cs", "hunks": [ { "oldStart": 137, "oldCount": 7, "newStart": 137, "newCount": 7, "header": "@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@ public class AiArtifactSource : ITenantOwned", "lines": [ { "oldNumber": 137, "newNumber": 137, "text": "    public string Label { get; set; } = \"\";" }, { "oldNumber": 138, "newNumber": 138, "text": "}" }, { "oldNumber": 139, "newNumber": 139 }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 140, "text": "/// \u003csummary\u003eImmutable redacted metadata for one AI invocation attempt.\u003c/summary\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 140, "text": "/// \u003csummary\u003eImmutable metadata for one AI invocation attempt, including rejected provider output for diagnosis.\u003c/summary\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 141, "newNumber": 141, "text": "public class AiAuditEvent : ITenantOwned" }, { "oldNumber": 142, "newNumber": 142, "text": "{" }, { "oldNumber": 143, "newNumber": 143, "text": "    public Guid Id { get; set; }" } ] }, { "oldStart": 164, "oldCount": 6, "newStart": 164, "newCount": 7, "header": "@@ -164,6 +164,7 @@ public class AiAuditEvent : ITenantOwned", "lines": [ { "oldNumber": 164, "newNumber": 164, "text": "    public int? ProviderStatusCode { get; set; }" }, { "oldNumber": 165, "newNumber": 165, "text": "    public string? ProviderFinishReason { get; set; }" }, { "oldNumber": 166, "newNumber": 166, "text": "    public string? ProviderRequestId { get; set; }" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 167, "text": "    public string? ProviderResponse { get; set; }" }, { "oldNumber": 167, "newNumber": 168, "text": "    public decimal EstimatedCost { get; set; }" }, { "oldNumber": 168, "newNumber": 169, "text": "    public DateTime StartedAt { get; set; }" }, { "oldNumber": 169, "newNumber": 170, "text": "    public DateTime CompletedAt { get; set; }" } ] } ] }
{ "path": "src/AndrewCrm.Web/Pages/Admin/AiAudit.cshtml", "hunks": [ { "oldStart": 4, "oldCount": 20, "newStart": 4, "newCount": 20, "header": "@@ -4,20 +4,20 @@", "lines": [ { "oldNumber": 4, "newNumber": 4, "text": "    ViewData[\"Title\"] = \"AI audit break-glass\";" }, { "oldNumber": 5, "newNumber": 5, "text": "    ViewData[\"Nav\"] = \"admin\";" }, { "oldNumber": 6, "newNumber": 6, "text": "}" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 7, "text": "\u003cdiv class=\"page-head\"\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"kicker\"\u003ePlatform ┬╖ Break-glass\u003c/div\u003e\u003ch1\u003eRedacted AI diagnostics\u003c/h1\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 8, "text": "    \u003cp class=\"sub\"\u003eAccess requires a recorded reason. This view never exposes contacts, actors, source references, prompts, model output, or mappings.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 7, "text": "\u003cdiv class=\"page-head\"\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"kicker\"\u003ePlatform ┬╖ Break-glass\u003c/div\u003e\u003ch1\u003eAI diagnostics\u003c/h1\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 8, "text": "    \u003cp class=\"sub\"\u003eAccess requires a recorded reason. Validation-rejected provider responses are shown and may contain model-generated sensitive content.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 9, "newNumber": 9, "text": "\u003cdiv class=\"panel panel-pad\"\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 10, "newNumber": 10, "text": "    \u003cform method=\"post\"\u003e\u003cdiv asp-validation-summary=\"All\" class=\"validation-summary\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 11, "newNumber": 11, "text": "        \u003clabel asp-for=\"TenantId\"\u003eTenant\u003c/label\u003e\u003cselect asp-for=\"TenantId\" required\u003e\u003coption value=\"\"\u003eSelect tenant\u003c/option\u003e@foreach (var tenant in Model.Tenants) { \u003coption value=\"@tenant.Id\"\u003e@tenant.Name\u003c/option\u003e }\u003c/select\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 12, "newNumber": 12, "text": "        \u003clabel asp-for=\"Reason\"\u003eBreak-glass reason\u003c/label\u003e\u003ctextarea asp-for=\"Reason\" rows=\"3\" required minlength=\"10\"\u003e\u003c/textarea\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 13, "text": "        \u003cdiv class=\"form-actions\"\u003e\u003cbutton class=\"btn btn-danger\"\u003eOpen redacted diagnostics\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 13, "text": "        \u003cdiv class=\"form-actions\"\u003e\u003cbutton class=\"btn btn-danger\"\u003eOpen diagnostics\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 14, "newNumber": 14, "text": "    \u003c/form\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 15, "newNumber": 15, "text": "\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 16, "newNumber": 16, "text": "@if (Model.Entries.Count \u003e 0)" }, { "oldNumber": 17, "newNumber": 17, "text": "{" }, { "oldNumber": 18, "newNumber": 18, "text": "    var telemetry = Model.Telemetry!;" }, { "oldNumber": 19, "newNumber": 19, "text": "    \u003cdiv class=\"panel panel-pad\"\u003e\u003ch2\u003eAggregate telemetry\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp class=\"sub\"\u003e@telemetry.InvocationCount calls ┬╖ @telemetry.AverageLatencyMs.ToString(\"N0\") ms average / @telemetry.P95LatencyMs.ToString(\"N0\") ms p95 ┬╖ @telemetry.InputTokens input / @telemetry.OutputTokens output tokens ┬╖ @telemetry.EstimatedCost.ToString(\"N6\") estimated cost\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"sub\"\u003e@telemetry.ValidationFailures validation failures ┬╖ @telemetry.ProviderFailures provider failures ┬╖ @telemetry.SafetyOutcomes safety outcomes ┬╖ @telemetry.RateLimitedOutcomes rate or spend-limit outcomes\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 20, "text": "    \u003cdiv class=\"panel table-wrap\"\u003e\u003ctable class=\"grid grid-stack\"\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eCompleted\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eTenant / treatment\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eSafe reason\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eDeployment metadata\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eRetry / cost\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eCorrelation\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 21, "text": "    @foreach (var entry in Model.Entries) { \u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@entry.CompletedAt.ToString(\"u\")\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e@entry.TenantId\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e@entry.Feature ┬╖ @entry.PromptVersion\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@(entry.SafeReasonCode ?? \"ΓÇö\")\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@entry.Provider ┬╖ @entry.Deployment ┬╖ @entry.Model ┬╖ @entry.Region@if (entry.ProviderStatusCode.HasValue) { \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sub\"\u003eHTTP @entry.ProviderStatusCode ┬╖ @(entry.ProviderFinishReason ?? \"no finish reason\") ┬╖ @entry.ReasoningTokens reasoning\u003c/span\u003e }\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@entry.RetryCount retries ┬╖ @entry.EstimatedCost.ToString(\"N6\")\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e@entry.CorrelationId\u003c/code\u003e@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(entry.ProviderRequestId)) { \u003cbr /\u003e\u003ccode\u003e@entry.ProviderRequestId\u003c/code\u003e }\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e }" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 20, "text": "    \u003cdiv class=\"panel table-wrap\"\u003e\u003ctable class=\"grid grid-stack\"\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eCompleted\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eTenant / treatment\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eSafe reason\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eDeployment metadata\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eRetry / cost\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eProvider response\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eCorrelation\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 21, "text": "    @foreach (var entry in Model.Entries) { \u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@entry.CompletedAt.ToString(\"u\")\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e@entry.TenantId\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e@entry.Feature ┬╖ @entry.PromptVersion\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@(entry.SafeReasonCode ?? \"ΓÇö\")\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@entry.Provider ┬╖ @entry.Deployment ┬╖ @entry.Model ┬╖ @entry.Region@if (entry.ProviderStatusCode.HasValue) { \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sub\"\u003eHTTP @entry.ProviderStatusCode ┬╖ @(entry.ProviderFinishReason ?? \"no finish reason\") ┬╖ @entry.ReasoningTokens reasoning\u003c/span\u003e }\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e@entry.RetryCount retries ┬╖ @entry.EstimatedCost.ToString(\"N6\")\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd class=\"ai-provider-response\"\u003e@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(entry.ProviderResponse)) { \u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003eView response\u003c/summary\u003e\u003cpre\u003e@entry.ProviderResponse\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/details\u003e } else { \u003cspan\u003eΓÇö\u003c/span\u003e }\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e@entry.CorrelationId\u003c/code\u003e@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(entry.ProviderRequestId)) { \u003cbr /\u003e\u003ccode\u003e@entry.ProviderRequestId\u003c/code\u003e }\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e }" }, { "oldNumber": 22, "newNumber": 22, "text": "    \u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e" }, { "oldNumber": 23, "newNumber": 23, "text": "}" } ] } ] }
{ "path": "src/AndrewCrm.Web/Pages/Admin/AiAudit.cshtml.cs", "hunks": [ { "oldStart": 19, "oldCount": 7, "newStart": 19, "newCount": 7, "header": "@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ public sealed class AiAuditModel : PageModel", "lines": [ { "oldNumber": 19, "newNumber": 19, "text": "    }" }, { "oldNumber": 20, "newNumber": 20 }, { "oldNumber": 21, "newNumber": 21, "text": "    public List\u003cTenant\u003e Tenants { get; private set; } = [];" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_REMOVED", "oldNumber": 22, "text": "    public List\u003cRedactedAiAuditEntry\u003e Entries { get; private set; } = [];" }, { "kind": "DIFF_LINE_KIND_ADDED", "newNumber": 22, "text": "    public List\u003cAiAuditEntry\u003e Entries { get; private set; } = [];" }, { "oldNumber": 23, "newNumber": 23, "text": "    public AiTelemetrySummary? Telemetry { get; private set; }" }, { "oldNumber": 24, "newNumber": 24, "text": "    [BindProperty] public Guid TenantId { get; set; }" }, { "oldNumber": 25, "newNumber": 25, "text": "    [BindProperty] public string Reason { get; set; } = \"\";" } ] } ] }
